From: AROS eza port maintainers
Date: 2026-10-21
Subject: [PATCH] Keep directory error kind and status through tree output
Repository: eza
Base-Commit: 98442ab17c2c3738701b62a7e060b1431ae2d6ea
Preceding-Patches: 0001 0002 0003
Upstream-Status: candidate (all platforms)
Scope: src/main.rs, src/output/details.rs; exit codes 1 (runtime) and 13
(permission denied) as already defined by eza.

0002 made tree rendering report child read failures as one generic
io::Error::other, which print_files then propagated with "?" as if output had
failed: later operands were skipped and a permission failure became code 1.
Carry the first error (a permission error wins) as a typed
DirectoryReadError with its original kind, treat it as a status rather than
an output failure, combine with max(), and never lower an earlier nonzero
status when a later directory is denied.

Verification: host unit tests tree_failure_keeps_kind_and_status and
tree_permission_error_does_not_skip_later_operand (src/main.rs).
Removal: drop with 0002 when upstream propagates directory errors itself.

